        "The evolution of virtual reality shows how technological advances have transformed the way we interact with digital environments. What began as experiments to improve visual perception now has applications in education, medicine, industry and entertainment. Its integration with new technologies opens up possibilities for continuing to develop more realistic, interactive and useful experiences in the future.",

